power: supply: axp2202: stock charger setup, fuel gauge model, charge state

The Brick's telemetry driver relied on whatever the last OS left in the
AXP2202: the fuel gauge only reported a capacity if TrimUI's firmware had
loaded its battery model since the battery was last disconnected, and the
charge voltage, termination current and NTC/JEITA windows were never set.
Status was Charging or Unknown, never Full or Discharging.

Do what the stock 4.9 axp2202_battery/axp2202_usb_power probe does
(disassembled from TrimUI's kernel), with the values from TrimUI's device
tree:

 - charge voltage 4.2 V (pmu_init_chgvol; probe fails if it does not read
   back), termination 128 mA, pre-charge code 2, VINDPM 3.96 V
   (pmu_usbad_vol 4000 mV);
 - TS pin on the NTC at 50 uA, charge window 0..50 C, work window
   -10..60 C, JEITA with reduced current in the cool and warm windows;
 - gauge warning levels 5 % / 0 %;
 - when the gauge's "model loaded" mark (0xa2 bit 4) is clear, write the
   128-byte battery model (axp2202-parameter/battery-model, now
   trimui,battery-model in the DTS) through the BROM window, verify it,
   set the mark and restart the gauge MCU (charging paused for ~1 s);
 - every poll, the stock coulomb-counter overflow check (indirect gauge
   register 0x2e), rate limited to one gauge reset per 10 minutes.

Report status like stock, made explicit: Discharging without VBUS,
Charging in pre/CC/CV, Full on charge-done or a full gauge on VBUS,
Not charging otherwise. Capacity rejects stock's "100 % below 3.45 V"
case as no data instead of 0, so a shutdown policy never acts on it.
Add time_to_empty_now/time_to_full_now (gauge, minutes, median of three),
constant_charge_voltage(_max), voltage_max_design, charge_term_current,
charge_full_design (3000 mAh, pmu_battery_cap) and technology.

The MFD regmap gains the registers this needs; the BROM and indirect data
windows are precious so a debugfs dump cannot advance them.

